    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0403" n="391" xml:id="pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A Recruiting/224: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-04T15:00:00+09:00">June 4, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>650. The Department’s instructions are respectfully requested as to whether, in
                    view of the provisions of the Neutrality Act,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d389-f1"/>
                    neutrality proclamation as published in Radio Bulletin No. 209, September 5,
                        1939,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d389-f2"/> and other provisions of law, the
                    enlistment in China (with its extraterritorial aspects) of American citizens in
                    the British armed forces is a lawful act, those Americans upon enlistment
                    presumably to proceed ultimately to combat zones.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Chungking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d389-f1" n="11" xml:id="d389-f1-content">
                <p>Approved November 4, 1939; 54 Stat. 4.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d389-f2" n="12" xml:id="d389-f2-content">
                <p>See Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, September 9, 1939,
                    p. 203.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
